@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title Benchmarking methodology (data-driven optimization protocol)
start
:pin CPU affinity
+ set cores to max frequency;<<#F1F3F5>>
:warm up
(prime caches / branch predictors);<<#F1F3F5>>
:perf record --call-graph lbr
(or criterion, when added);<<#FFF3BF>>
:tee output to a file
(run once, analyze many);<<#F1F3F5>>
:generate + analyze perf report
in parallel;<<#FFF3BF>>
stop
note right
  <b>Documented current gap:</b> runnable benchmarks
  are not yet wired up. <i>criterion 0.5</i> is a
  dev-dependency, but both <latex>[[bench]]</latex>
  targets in Cargo.toml are commented out
  ("Benchmarks will be added when implementations
  are complete"). Until then the amber steps use
  <i>perf</i> directly.
end note
legend right
  |= colour |= role |
  |<#FFF3BF>| measurement / profiling tool |
  |<#F1F3F5>| setup / bookkeeping step |
endlegend
@enduml
